/-
# Varieties without a finite basis of identities (Kourovka Notebook Problem 2.39)

Kourovka Notebook, Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.39 (A. I. Mal'cev): does there exist a
non-finitely-axiomatizable variety of (a) (H. Neumann) groups? (b) associative rings (the Specht
problem)? (c) Lie rings?
-/

module

public import Batteries.Util.ProofWanted
public import WantedExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared

@[expose] public section

namespace MathlibExt.Algebra.NonFinitelyBasedVarietiesKourovka2Problem39Wanted

/-!
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.39 (A. I.
Mal'cev). UnsolvedMath record UM-00700112 (`KOU-2.39`), dataset ulamai/UnsolvedMath v1.8.0.

A variety is represented through the identities of an algebra: the variety generated by an algebra
is finitely based exactly when finitely many of its identities imply all of them in every algebra of
the signature (all algebras in `Type`), and a variety is finitely based exactly when the algebra
generating it (its free algebra of countable rank) has this property. Group words are elements of
`FreeGroup ℕ`; ring identities are elements of the free non-unital associative ring `MonoidAlgebra ℤ
(FreeSemigroup ℕ)` (associative rings are not assumed unital, the convention of the Mal'cev school
and of the Specht problem); Lie ring identities are elements of the free Lie ring `FreeLieAlgebra ℤ
ℕ`. These definitions are shared with the other varieties entries in
`WantedExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared`. Each part is stated for the variety generated by a
single algebra, which loses nothing: every variety is generated by its free algebra of countable
rank.
-/

open MathlibExt.Algebra.VarietyIdentitiesShared

/-- Kourovka 2.39(a) (H. Neumann; A. I. Mal'cev): some variety of groups is not finitely based,
stated for the variety generated by a single group (every variety is generated by its free group
of countable rank). -/
def nonFinitelyBasedGroupVarietyExists : Prop :=
  ∃ (G : Type) (_ : Group G), ¬ GroupLawsFinitelyBased G

/-- Kourovka 2.39(b) (the Specht problem): some variety of associative rings is not finitely
based. -/
def nonFinitelyBasedRingVarietyExists : Prop :=
  ∃ (A : Type) (_ : NonUnitalRing A), ¬ RingIdentitiesFinitelyBased A

/-- Kourovka 2.39(c): some variety of Lie rings is not finitely based. -/
def nonFinitelyBasedLieRingVarietyExists : Prop :=
  ∃ (L : Type) (_ : LieRing L), ¬ LieIdentitiesFinitelyBased L

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.39(a) "Yes" (Adian; Ol'shanskii, 1970). Ol'shanskii
proved there are continuum many varieties of groups (Drensky's survey, Theorem 7.1), while finitely
based varieties are countably many; Adian gave an independent infinite system of laws (Theorem 7.3).
Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka
Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.39 (A. I.
Mal'cev); resolution: S. I. Adian, Math. USSR-Izv. 4 (1970), 721-739; A. Yu. Ol'shanskii, Math.
USSR-Izv. 4 (1970), 381-389; A. Ya. Belov, Sb. Math. 191 (2000), 329-340; A. V. Grishin, Fundam.
Prikl. Mat. 5 (1999), 101-118; V. V. Shchigolev, Fundam. Prikl. Mat. 5 (1999), 307-312; M. R.
Vaughan-Lee, Quart. J. Math. 21 (1970), 297-308; survey: V. Drensky, Finite basis problem for
varieties of algebraic systems, arXiv:2602.18805 (2026), Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.39: a), b), c)
Yes; Drensky's survey, Theorems 7.1 and 7.3 (groups: Ol'shanskii, continuum many varieties; Adian,
an independent system of laws), Theorem 8.1 (Lie algebras over a field of characteristic 2,
Vaughan-Lee) and Theorems 9.1-9.3 (associative algebras in positive characteristic: Belov, Grishin,
Shchigolev), https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.18805.
-/
public theorem_wanted nonFinitelyBasedGroupVarietyExists_holds : nonFinitelyBasedGroupVarietyExists

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.39(b), the Specht problem for associative rings, "Yes"
(Belov; Grishin; Shchigolev, 1999): over fields of positive characteristic there are varieties of
associative algebras without a finite basis of identities (Drensky's survey, Theorems 9.1-9.3;
Grishin's example consists of nil algebras, so it is a variety of non-unital algebras), and an
algebra over `𝔽_p` is a ring satisfying `p x = 0`. Over fields of characteristic `0` every variety
of associative algebras is finitely based (Kemer). Source: E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.),
Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026),
Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.39 (A. I. Mal'cev); resolution: S. I. Adian, Math. USSR-Izv. 4
(1970), 721-739; A. Yu. Ol'shanskii, Math. USSR-Izv. 4 (1970), 381-389; A. Ya. Belov, Sb. Math. 191
(2000), 329-340; A. V. Grishin, Fundam. Prikl. Mat. 5 (1999), 101-118; V. V. Shchigolev, Fundam.
Prikl. Mat. 5 (1999), 307-312; M. R. Vaughan-Lee, Quart. J. Math. 21 (1970), 297-308; survey: V.
Drensky, Finite basis problem for varieties of algebraic systems, arXiv:2602.18805 (2026), Kourovka
Archive, Problem 2.39: a), b), c) Yes; Drensky's survey, Theorems 7.1 and 7.3 (groups: Ol'shanskii,
continuum many varieties; Adian, an independent system of laws), Theorem 8.1 (Lie algebras over a
field of characteristic 2, Vaughan-Lee) and Theorems 9.1-9.3 (associative algebras in positive
characteristic: Belov, Grishin, Shchigolev), https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.18805.
-/
public theorem_wanted nonFinitelyBasedRingVarietyExists_holds : nonFinitelyBasedRingVarietyExists

/--
Resolved true: the Kourovka Archive answers 2.39(c) "Yes" (Vaughan-Lee, 1970), whose variety of Lie
algebras over a field of characteristic `2` defined by `[[x₁, x₂], [x₃, x₄], x₅] = 0` and `[[x₁, …,
xₙ], [x₁, x₂]] = 0` (`n ≥ 3`) is not finitely based (Drensky's survey, Theorem 8.1). Source: E. I.
Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), Unsolved Problems in Group Theory: The Kourovka Notebook, 21st
issue, arXiv:1401.0300v49 (2026), Archive of Solved Problems, Problem 2.39 (A. I. Mal'cev);
resolution: S. I. Adian, Math. USSR-Izv. 4 (1970), 721-739; A. Yu. Ol'shanskii, Math. USSR-Izv. 4
(1970), 381-389; A. Ya. Belov, Sb. Math. 191 (2000), 329-340; A. V. Grishin, Fundam. Prikl. Mat. 5
(1999), 101-118; V. V. Shchigolev, Fundam. Prikl. Mat. 5 (1999), 307-312; M. R. Vaughan-Lee, Quart.
J. Math. 21 (1970), 297-308; survey: V. Drensky, Finite basis problem for varieties of algebraic
systems, arXiv:2602.18805 (2026), Kourovka Archive, Problem 2.39: a), b), c) Yes; Drensky's survey,
Theorems 7.1 and 7.3 (groups: Ol'shanskii, continuum many varieties; Adian, an independent system of
laws), Theorem 8.1 (Lie algebras over a field of characteristic 2, Vaughan-Lee) and Theorems 9.1-9.3
(associative algebras in positive characteristic: Belov, Grishin, Shchigolev),
https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.18805.
-/
public theorem_wanted nonFinitelyBasedLieRingVarietyExists_holds :
    nonFinitelyBasedLieRingVarietyExists

end MathlibExt.Algebra.NonFinitelyBasedVarietiesKourovka2Problem39Wanted
